# Lock poison recovery consolidated onto one shared guard trait (2026-10-05)

== 1. What this batch replaces

`xai-grok-shell` read its `std::sync` locks in two moods. Some call sites recovered from poisoning on the
spot, some turned poisoning into a panic. This batch puts all of them on one pair of traits
(`crates/codegen/xai-grok-shell/src/util/shared_guard.rs`) so that the recovery policy lives in exactly one
place, and then gives the traits consumers that actually read a poisoned guard through shipped code.

  * 28 call sites that panicked on poisoning, in 11 files, were rewritten onto `lock_or_recover` /
    `read_or_recover` / `write_or_recover`. Four of those 28 sit under `#[cfg(test)]`, so they were never
    production sites and the census does not move for them.
  * 10 call sites that already recovered, but each spelled `unwrap_or_else(PoisonError::into_inner)` by
    hand, were folded onto the same traits. These change no count at all: they did not panic before.
  * The 15 sites in `agent/models/startup_prefetch.rs` that the previous batch had routed through a
    module-private helper now call the shared trait too, and that helper is gone.
  * 17 new tests: 5 for the trait itself (`util/shared_guard_tests.rs`), 11 consumer tests in
    `tools/tool_context.rs`, `session/acp_session_impl/turn_task.rs`, `claude_import.rs`,
    `agent/auth_method.rs`, and 1 `#[tokio::test]` in `managed_config/tests.rs`.

== 2. The baseline cell went red before any mutation did, and it was the harness's fault

The matrix's first cell mutates nothing. It exists because every other cell is judged by one bit: did the
test command exit non-zero. Without an unmutated reading of the same command, "did not go red" has three
possible causes (no coverage, the command never reached that code, or the fix is genuinely unobserved) and
the exit code does not separate them. Round one's baseline cell aborted:

    B0: 0 site(s) mutated -> CAUGHT (expected survived) ** CONTRARY TO EXPECTATION ** exit=101

and inside that cell's captured output:

    thread 'session::acp_session::cancel_running_task_tests::handle_prompt_frames_interrupt_on_user_message' (2807178) has overflowed its stack
    fatal runtime error: stack overflow, aborting
    error: test failed, to rerun pass `-p xai-grok-shell --lib`

Nothing about this batch is involved. `scripts/verify-gates.sh` exports a stack floor for every gate and the
container exports the same value through `--env`, because the actor tests in this crate need more than the
harness default:

    RUST_MIN_STACK_DEFAULT=16777216
    export RUST_MIN_STACK="${RUST_MIN_STACK:-${RUST_MIN_STACK_DEFAULT}}"

The matrix had been launched with a bare `cargo test -p xai-grok-shell --lib`, which is not the command the
shipped runners run. With the floor exported, the same unmutated command is green, and that reading is the
one every later FULL cell is compared against:

    B0: 0 site(s) mutated -> SURVIVED (expected survived) as expected exit=0

The harness was then changed so this cannot recur silently: a red baseline aborts the whole run with its own
exit code instead of letting 29 later cells be judged against it, and a cell that disagrees with its
expectation now makes the run exit non-zero (it had been returning 0 unconditionally, so the first round's
nine disagreements printed their own warning into a green exit code).

== 3. Round one: 30 cells, 9 of them disagreeing with the expectation table

    matrix: 30 mutants, 22 caught, 8 survived, 9 contrary to expectation ['B0', 'T2', 'T7', 'C2', 'C4', 'A2', 'A4', 'G1', 'G2']

Two of the nine are the baseline and the two FULL cells (`G1`, `G2`) judged against it, all three explained
by section 2. The remaining six split into two honest categories, and they are not the same finding.

== 4. Three survivors sit in `#[cfg(test)]` helpers, which are not shipped code

`T2` is `BlockingWaitState::set_depth_for_test`, `C4` is `claude_import::reset_marker_cache_for_test`, `A4`
is `reset_runtime_api_key_for_test`. All three are `#[cfg(test)]` items with no shipped caller: the census
excludes `cfg(test)` spans, which is exactly why 28 rewritten sites moved `expect_prod` by 24 and not by 28.
A mutant inside a test-only helper is observable only through test code, and a test written to observe it
would have the test harness as its subject. These three are recorded as expected survivals with that reason
attached in the matrix's own expectation table rather than dropped from the batch:

    T2: 1 site(s) mutated -> SURVIVED (expected survived) as expected exit=0
        reason for expecting survival: tool_context.rs:90 is `set_depth_for_test`, a #[cfg(test)] setter: no shipped caller, so a mutant there is observable only through test code

== 5. Three survivors were real gaps in the tests, and they are now closed

`T7` is `BlockingWaitGuard::enter`, `C2` is the cache-filling write inside `is_claude_import_marked`, `A2` is
`set_runtime_api_key`. All three are production writes. The tests written for this batch reached the guard in
a poisoned state and then read or cleared it, but never wrote through it:

  * `the_wait_guard_still_counts_in_through_a_poisoned_state` poisons first and then enters a wait, because
    the depth is what makes `queue_input` take its send-now path; counting out alone left `enter` uncovered.
  * `a_poisoned_marker_cache_still_fills_itself_on_the_first_uncached_read` leaves the cache empty instead of
    seeding it, so the call has to read the marker from disk and store it through the poisoned guard. The
    expected value is whatever the file says, so the test holds with or without the marker set.
  * `a_poisoned_runtime_key_cell_still_answers_and_still_accepts_a_write` now publishes a key after the
    poisoning too; it had only cleared one, which left the publisher the auth flow actually calls uncovered.

    T7: 1 site(s) mutated -> CAUGHT (expected caught) as expected exit=101
        tools::tool_context::tests::the_wait_guard_still_counts_in_through_a_poisoned_state
    C2: 1 site(s) mutated -> CAUGHT (expected caught) as expected exit=101
        claude_import::tests::a_poisoned_marker_cache_still_fills_itself_on_the_first_uncached_read
    A2: 1 site(s) mutated -> CAUGHT (expected caught) as expected exit=101
        agent::auth_method::runtime_api_key_tests::a_poisoned_runtime_key_cell_still_answers_and_still_accepts_a_write

