Taken together the two rounds measure 29 mutants over the 28 rewritten sites plus the three recovery bodies
in the trait itself: 22 caught, 7 survived, none contrary to expectation. The 7 surviving cells cover 21
call sites, and the two big ones (`G1`, `G2`) are recorded as open work rather than being described as
unreachable: closing them needs a session actor that has published a prompt id, which no unit-test seam
constructs today.

== 7. The failure mode these sites had is an abort, not a test failure

Three of the rewritten sites are reached from a `Drop` that runs while the thread is already unwinding
(`BlockingWaitGuard::drop`, `TurnSubagentScopeGuard::drop`, and `FinishGuard::drop` from the previous batch).
A panic raised during unwinding cannot be caught, so the mutant does not fail one assertion, it kills the
test binary:

    thread 'tools::tool_context::tests::a_stale_guard_still_leaves_the_new_generation_alone_behind_a_poisoned_state' panicked
    panic in a destructor during cleanup
    thread caused non-unwinding panic. aborting.
    error: test failed, to rerun pass `-p xai-grok-shell --lib`
    Caused by:
      process didn't exit successfully: `target/debug/deps/xai_grok_shell-08161f36e816855b 'util::shared_guard' 'tools::tool_context' 'session::acp_session::turn_task' 'claude_import::' 'agent::models::startup_prefetch' 'agent::auth_method' managed_config` (signal: 6, SIGABRT: process abort signal)

(The binary path is the workspace's own `target/debug/deps` build output, written here relative to the
workspace root; the rest of the block is verbatim.)

That is scored as caught. Treating it as a flaky harness and retrying would throw away the exact behaviour
this batch removes.

== 8. Measurement, both readings taken from the current source

Before the change (recorded in the committed baseline at `1683249c`'s successor) and after, each a separate
scan rather than arithmetic:

    $ python3 scripts/ci/panic-site-census.py --check-baseline scripts/ci/panic-site-baseline.tsv
    baseline holds: 97 crates, 24 fewer production sites than recorded

    $ python3 scripts/ci/panic-site-census.py --write-baseline scripts/ci/panic-site-baseline.tsv
    wrote scripts/ci/panic-site-baseline.tsv (97 crates)

    -xai-grok-shell	23	110	28	13
    +xai-grok-shell	23	86	28	13

    $ python3 scripts/ci/panic-site-census.py --check-baseline scripts/ci/panic-site-baseline.tsv
    baseline holds: 97 crates, 0 fewer production sites than recorded

The columns are crate, `unwrap_prod`, `expect_prod`, `panic_prod`, `unsafe_prod`. `expect_prod` is the one
this batch moves, by 24: the 24 production `.expect("… poisoned …")` sites. Production `unwrap` (23),
`panic` (28) and `unsafe` (13) are untouched, which is the check that the batch did not silently move work
from one panic shape to another.

== 9. Test and gate readings

    $ cargo fmt --all --check
    (no output)

    $ RUST_MIN_STACK=16777216 cargo test -p xai-grok-shell --lib -- util::shared_guard tools::tool_context session::acp_session::turn_task claude_import:: agent::models::startup_prefetch agent::auth_method managed_config
    test result: ok. 125 passed; 0 failed; 1 ignored; 0 measured; 6806 filtered out; finished in 0.16s

    $ RUST_MIN_STACK=16777216 cargo test -p xai-grok-shell --lib
    (green; this is the B0 cell of round two, exit=0)

The filtered command is the fast cell's command, and the `125 passed` reading is what keeps that cell from
being vacuous: an empty filter match exits 0 in the same shape as a real pass.

== 10. Reproduce

    $ git clone . /tmp/repro && git -C /tmp/repro checkout --detach HEAD
    $ cd /tmp/repro
    $ python3 scripts/ci/panic-site-census.py --check-baseline scripts/ci/panic-site-baseline.tsv
    $ bash scripts/verify-gates.sh --with-build

The mutation matrix itself is not committed; it is a scratch tool. Its transcripts are the two files this
log quotes, kept under `{SCRATCH}` for the duration of the batch, and every cell restored its source from a
pristine copy with `cmp` verifying the bytes afterwards.
